enced by a main-plan epic (branch rule 2). |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|---------|----------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 (investigation); BRANCH-A-E007 or BRANCH-B-E007 (implementation, selected by E001 outcome) | All-or-nothing admission for multi-node training jobs. |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | E004 | Per-project GPU quota enforced at admission across PyTorchJob and RayJob. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | E005 | Queue position, quota consumption, and admission state visible in the Dashboard. |\n| HLR-4 | P1 | E002 (investigation); BRANCH-A-E008 or BRANCH-B-E008 + BRANCH-B-E009 (implementation, selected by E002 outcome) | Admin-defined preemption policy; semantics determined by E002. |\n| HLR-5 | P2 | E003 (investigation); E006 (implementation, gated by E003) | Topology-aware placement, contingent on topology discovery maturity. |\n\nAll five HLRs are covered; none orphaned.\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\n- All three strategy components (`Distributed Workloads`, `Training Operator`, `Dashboard`) exist verbatim in `.context/rhai-components.txt` and in `.context/architecture-context/` — no new-component onboarding chain is needed; all are Konflux-onboarded.\n- **Training Operator is passive for HLR-1/HLR-2**: per architecture context, the operator performs no scheduling — PyTorchJob admission flows through Kueue integration, and both Training Operator and Distributed Workloads are owned by the same team (Distributed Workloads). Validation that PyTorchJob workloads are admitted all-or-nothing and counted against project quota is therefore captured as acceptance criteria on the Distributed Workloads epics (E004 and the gang-admission branch epics), not as separate epics.\n- **Training Operator is active only for checkpoint-aware graceful preemption** (BRANCH-B-E009), where checkpoint/restart support requires operator/framework changes.\n- **RayJob/KubeRay work** falls under the canonical `Distributed Workloads` component (kuberay is 