{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-55a57246-b5f2-4c39-856d-2e6ea96319e4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89426ef5b77845cd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-_i7jam9k/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E004.md","content":"# Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission for training job types\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time for distributed training workloads, so that a project's PyTorchJob and RayJob submissions are counted against its GPU quota when they are admitted, rather than after pods land. It works through the platform's queueing layer (Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model), which is the admission point for both job types.\n\n## Description of dependencies\n\nThe admission-time enforcement approach depends on the outcome of the gang-admission semantics investigation: whether Kueue-native admission suffices or scheduler-plugin work is required changes where admission-time enforcement hooks in. This epic starts once that investigation resolves; the quota capability exists in either outcome but its implementation approach may be rewritten.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define and implement the per-project GPU quota model on the queueing layer's cluster-queue/local-queue structures, covering GPU resources consumed by PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n- Enforce quota at admission time: pending workloads that would exceed a project's GPU quota are not admitted until capacity/quota frees up, for both job types.\n- Integrate quota accounting across training job types so PyTorchJob and RayJob submissions from the same project count against the same GPU quota.\n- Provide configuration for admins to set per-project GPU quotas.\n- Validate that PyTorchJob workloads (training-operator integration) and RayJob workloads (kuberay integration) are both correctly counted and gated at admission — the training operator itself performs no scheduling, so this validation lands here as the owning team's acceptance criteria.\n- Expose quota consumption in a way the Dashboard can read (per-project queue and quota-consumption status on the workload/queue interfaces), as the data foundation for pending-job visibility.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A PyTorchJob or RayJob submission that would push a project past its configured GPU quota is held pending at admission time (not partially scheduled), and is admitted once quota frees up — verified for both job types.\n- Quota accounting is shared across job types: mixed PyTorchJob and RayJob submissions from one project count against the same per-project GPU quota.\n- Admins can configure per-project GPU quotas, and changes take effect on subsequent admissions without requiring a restart of running workloads.\n- PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads validate end-to-end against the enforced quota at representative sizes.\n- Quota-consumption state for a project is observable on the queueing layer's interfaces (readable for later Dashboard surfacing).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): Per-project GPU quota is enforced at admission time across training job types (PyTorchJob, RayJob) — primary coverage.\n- HLR-1 (P0): contributes the admission-time gating behavior (pending rather than partially scheduled) that the all-or-nothing admission work builds on.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47395,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89be6101d3983008","agent_id":"a87ab15cfd5e9f59c","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"42265fd0-d0ee-41b5-9266-8c60b3c25bc5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:22:50.365Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
