{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bbfafec9-bb29-47a9-9409-d974b6bda5ca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ca554a7690f2909","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-_i7jam9k/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E005.md","content":"# Pending-job queue visibility in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers user-facing visibility into the queueing state of pending distributed training jobs in the Dashboard: users can see the queue position, quota consumption, and admission state of their pending jobs. The Dashboard reads workload and queue state from the Kubernetes API (Workload CRs and queueing-layer status); it owns no data plane.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a Dashboard surface (within the existing distributed-workload status views) showing, per pending job: queue position, the project's GPU quota consumption, and admission state.\n- Read queue position, admission state, and quota consumption from the queueing layer's workload/queue interfaces and per-project quota model established by the admission-time quota enforcement work.\n- Present admission state for pending jobs (e.g., pending, awaiting quota, admitted) in project-scoped views, respecting OpenShift OAuth project-scoped RBAC.\n- Gate the visibility feature behind the Dashboard's per-component feature flags/defaults mechanism where appropriate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can select a pending training job in the Dashboard and see its queue position, the project's GPU quota consumption, and its admission state.\n- The displayed state matches the queueing layer's actual workload/queue status for pending PyTorchJob and RayJob jobs (verified against the CR/metrics source).\n- Views are project-scoped: a user sees queue and quota information only for projects they can access under OpenShift RBAC.\n- The feature can be enabled/disabled via the Dashboard's existing per-component feature-flag configuration.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): Users can see queue position, quota consumption, and admission state for their pending jobs in the Dashboard — primary coverage.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48750,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89be6101d3983008","agent_id":"a87ab15cfd5e9f59c","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"0d0a270c-99ad-44b5-808d-b169dcd05288","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:23:14.049Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
