{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-451e4faa-bee7-4615-9fb7-af97339da49b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87234d5c9fd3bca6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-_i7jam9k/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E006.md","content":"# Topology-aware GPU placement for training workloads\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers topology-aware job placement for distributed training workloads: when the cluster exposes GPU topology information, job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes (e.g., keeping a job's GPUs within NVLink domains) to avoid the throughput loss reported on mixed fleets. This capability is contingent on the maturity assessment of node topology discovery (currently Tech Preview); if the discovery layer is not mature enough to build on this release, this epic is removed and the work is deferred.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enable the queueing layer's topology-aware scheduling support so that admitted training workloads prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster exposes topology information.\n- Consume node topology discovery data (Tech Preview) as the placement signal; degrade gracefully to default placement on clusters that do not expose topology information.\n- Cover PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n- Placement is a preference, not a hard requirement: when topology-aligned capacity is unavailable, jobs still admit per the all-or-nothing and quota rules rather than starving.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- On a cluster exposing GPU topology information, a training job's pods are placed with topology-aligned preference (validated against the exposed topology, e.g., NVLink domain alignment) when such capacity exists.\n- On a cluster not exposing topology information, jobs admit normally with default placement and no errors attributable to topology awareness.\n- Topology preference never blocks admission that the all-or-nothing and quota rules would otherwise grant (preference, not gate).\n- Placement behavior is validated for both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P2): Job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster exposes topology information — primary coverage.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49296,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89be6101d3983008","agent_id":"a87ab15cfd5e9f59c","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"4691cf30-b8d1-4461-931c-8560a7b86810","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:23:26.881Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
