{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b18598845a3a2744","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n3\ttitle: Assess maturity of node topology discovery for topology-aware placement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Assess maturity of node topology discovery for topology-aware placement\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's open question on topology-aware placement: the node topology discovery it depends on is only Tech Preview, and it must be determined whether it is mature enough to build the topology-aware placement capability on in this release. The answer decides whether the placement work exists at all in this release.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Assess the current state of node topology discovery (Tech Preview): API surface stability, known defects, upgrade history, and the provider's stated path to general availability.\n34\t- Evaluate how the queueing layer's topology-aware scheduling support (itself Tech Preview in the platform) consumes the discovery data, and its readiness for GPU-topology-aligned placement (e.g., NVLink domain alignment).\n35\t- Identify gaps and risks: data correctness on the targeted GPU node types, behavior across node upgrades, and rework cost if the discovery API changes at general availability.\n36\t- Deliverable: a go/no-go recommendation for building topology-aware placement this release, with the evidence and the conditions under which the placement work should be deferred.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A written assessment of node topology discovery maturity exists, covering API stability, known defects, GPU-node-type coverage, and the upgrade/GA path, each with cited evidence from the public record (documentation, release notes, issue tracker).\n41\t- A go/no-go recommendation is recorded for building topology-aware placement this release, with explicit criteria and the rework risk if the discovery API changes at GA.\n42\t\n43\t## HLR Traceability\n44\t\n45\t- HLR-5 (P2): Job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster exposes topology information. This investigation determines whether the topology discovery HLR-5 depends on is mature enough to build on this release, and gates the HLR-5 implementation.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97427b6cdc973e21","agent_id":"a8f861f4d9cfa2f37","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"40bb4033-2387-4409-ba4e-3c53c1d90b47","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:29:34.421Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b18598845a3a2744","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
