{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd5e74255874a40d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n3\ttitle: Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission for training job types\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the gang-admission investigation selects the scheduler-plugin\n15\t    path, the admission-time quota enforcement approach is rewritten to hook the per-project\n16\t    quota at the new admission point; the quota capability itself remains.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 5\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission for training job types\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time for distributed training workloads, so that a project's PyTorchJob and RayJob submissions are counted against its GPU quota when they are admitted, rather than after pods land. It works through the platform's queueing layer (Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model), which is the admission point for both job types. The admission-time enforcement approach depends on the outcome of the gang-admission semantics investigation: whether Kueue-native admission suffices or scheduler-plugin work is required changes where admission-time enforcement hooks in, so this epic starts once that investigation resolves; the quota capability exists in either outcome but its implementation approach may be rewritten.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define and implement the per-project GPU quota model on the queueing layer's cluster-queue/local-queue structures, covering GPU resources consumed by PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n43\t- Enforce quota at admission time: pending workloads that would exceed a project's GPU quota are not admitted until capacity/quota frees up, for both job types.\n44\t- Integrate quota accounting across training job types so PyTorchJob and RayJob submissions from the same project count against the same GPU quota.\n45\t- Provide configuration for admins to set per-project GPU quotas.\n46\t- Validate that PyTorchJob workloads (training-operator integration) and RayJob workloads (kuberay integration) are both correctly counted and gated at admission — the training operator itself performs no scheduling, so this validation lands here as the owning team's acceptance criteria.\n47\t- Expose quota consumption in a way the Dashboard can read (per-project queue and quota-consumption status on the workload/queue interfaces), as the data foundation for pending-job visibility.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A PyTorchJob or RayJob submission that would push a project past its configured GPU quota is held pending at admission time (not partially scheduled), and is admitted once quota frees up — verified for both job types.\n52\t- Quota accounting is shared across job types: mixed PyTorchJob and RayJob submissions from one project count against the same per-project GPU quota.\n53\t- Admins can configure per-project GPU quotas, and changes take effect on subsequent admissions without requiring a restart of running workloads.\n54\t- PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads validate end-to-end against the enforced quota at representative sizes.\n55\t- Quota-consumption state for a project is observable on the queueing layer's interfaces (readable for later Dashboard surfacing).\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-2 (P0): Per-project GPU quota is enforced at admission time across training job types (PyTorchJob, RayJob) — primary coverage.\n60\t- HLR-1 (P0): contributes the admission-time gating behavior (pending rather than partially scheduled) that the all-or-nothing admission work builds on.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97427b6cdc973e21","agent_id":"a8f861f4d9cfa2f37","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"a8c5034c-04b6-4eca-a3f8-45926a05dc1d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:29:38.241Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd5e74255874a40d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
