{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b23770fe3598746","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E005\n3\ttitle: Pending-job queue visibility in the Dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Pending-job queue visibility in the Dashboard\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers user-facing visibility into the queueing state of pending distributed training jobs in the Dashboard: users can see the queue position, quota consumption, and admission state of their pending jobs. The Dashboard reads workload and queue state from the Kubernetes API (Workload CRs and queueing-layer status); it owns no data plane.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Add a Dashboard surface (within the existing distributed-workload status views) showing, per pending job: queue position, the project's GPU quota consumption, and admission state.\n39\t- Read queue position, admission state, and quota consumption from the queueing layer's workload/queue interfaces and per-project quota model established by the admission-time quota enforcement work.\n40\t- Present admission state for pending jobs (e.g., pending, awaiting quota, admitted) in project-scoped views, respecting OpenShift OAuth project-scoped RBAC.\n41\t- Gate the visibility feature behind the Dashboard's per-component feature flags/defaults mechanism where appropriate.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A user can select a pending training job in the Dashboard and see its queue position, the project's GPU quota consumption, and its admission state.\n46\t- The displayed state matches the queueing layer's actual workload/queue status for pending PyTorchJob and RayJob jobs (verified against the CR/metrics source).\n47\t- Views are project-scoped: a user sees queue and quota information only for projects they can access under OpenShift RBAC.\n48\t- The feature can be enabled/disabled via the Dashboard's existing per-component feature-flag configuration.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-3 (P1): Users can see queue position, quota consumption, and admission state for their pending jobs in the Dashboard — primary coverage.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97427b6cdc973e21","agent_id":"a8f861f4d9cfa2f37","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"a8ec3d16-0e9b-4774-99ab-ce31040cd7f0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:29:39.525Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b23770fe3598746","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
