{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a09b9f9d670832c8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E006\n3\ttitle: Topology-aware GPU placement for training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: remove\n14\t  fallback_approach: If node topology discovery (Tech Preview) is assessed as not\n15\t    mature enough to build on this release, this epic is removed and topology-aware\n16\t    placement is deferred to a later release.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Topology-aware GPU placement for training workloads\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers topology-aware job placement for distributed training workloads: when the cluster exposes GPU topology information, job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes (e.g., keeping a job's GPUs within NVLink domains) to avoid the throughput loss reported on mixed fleets. This capability is contingent on the maturity assessment of node topology discovery (currently Tech Preview); if the discovery layer is not mature enough to build on this release, this epic is removed and the work is deferred.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Enable the queueing layer's topology-aware scheduling support so that admitted training workloads prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster exposes topology information.\n43\t- Consume node topology discovery data (Tech Preview) as the placement signal; degrade gracefully to default placement on clusters that do not expose topology information.\n44\t- Cover PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n45\t- Placement is a preference, not a hard requirement: when topology-aligned capacity is unavailable, jobs still admit per the all-or-nothing and quota rules rather than starving.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- On a cluster exposing GPU topology information, a training job's pods are placed with topology-aligned preference (validated against the exposed topology, e.g., NVLink domain alignment) when such capacity exists.\n50\t- On a cluster not exposing topology information, jobs admit normally with default placement and no errors attributable to topology awareness.\n51\t- Topology preference never blocks admission that the all-or-nothing and quota rules would otherwise grant (preference, not gate).\n52\t- Placement behavior is validated for both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-5 (P2): Job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster exposes topology information — primary coverage.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97427b6cdc973e21","agent_id":"a8f861f4d9cfa2f37","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"9b149058-e1d0-4e5f-ba29-dd1e61c752ee","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:29:40.622Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a09b9f9d670832c8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
