{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b563d299672a0e68","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E007\n3\ttitle: Kueue-native gang admission hardening for training jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation finds Kueue-native gang-admission semantics\n16\t    insufficient at target scale, this branch is dropped in favor of the coscheduling\n17\t    scheduler-plugin branch.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Kueue-native gang admission hardening for training jobs\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis branch epic implements all-or-nothing (gang) admission for multi-node training jobs using the queueing layer's native admission semantics (waitForPodsReady), selected when the gang-admission investigation finds the native semantics sufficient at target scale — possibly with tuning. No pods of a training job occupy GPUs while the remaining pods wait; a job is either fully admitted or held pending.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Configure and tune the queueing layer's waitForPodsReady gang-admission semantics for PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads at target scale (timeouts, pod-readiness parameters, requeue behavior on failure), informed by the investigation's measurements.\n43\t- Ensure partially schedulable jobs are not admitted piecemeal: no partial GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods.\n44\t- Ensure jobs that cannot be fully admitted within the configured timeout are requeued rather than dying partially scheduled.\n45\t- Validate gang admission end-to-end for PyTorchJob (training-operator workloads) and RayJob workloads at representative multi-node GPU sizes under queue contention.\n46\t- Rollback safety: admission-behavior changes are configuration-based and reversible so existing workload admission can be restored without code rollback.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- A multi-node PyTorchJob or RayJob is admitted all-or-nothing: no partial GPU occupation is observed while waiting for remaining pods, verified at target scale under queue contention.\n51\t- A job that cannot be fully admitted within the configured timeout is requeued (not left partially scheduled and not killed mid-partial-schedule).\n52\t- Configuration is reversible: reverting the admission settings restores prior admission behavior for running and pending workloads.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-1 (P0): Multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing — primary coverage, via the Kueue-native path selected by the gang-admission investigation.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97427b6cdc973e21","agent_id":"a8f861f4d9cfa2f37","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"2da711eb-2e72-4882-b4f5-eb2489e033bc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:29:44.702Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b563d299672a0e68","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
