{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8643790898e1c3cc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E007\n3\ttitle: Coscheduling scheduler-plugin enablement for gang admission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation finds Kueue-native gang-admission semantics\n16\t    sufficient, this branch is dropped in favor of the Kueue-native admission branch.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Coscheduling scheduler-plugin enablement for gang admission\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tThis branch epic implements all-or-nothing (gang) admission for multi-node training jobs by enabling a coscheduling scheduler plugin in the platform, selected when the gang-admission investigation finds the queueing layer's native semantics insufficient at target scale. The platform does not currently ship a scheduler plugin for gang scheduling (Volcano is not shipped), so this path provisions and integrates the plugin alongside the queueing layer's admission.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Enable a coscheduling scheduler plugin in the platform's scheduler configuration so that pods of a training job are scheduled as a group (all-or-nothing at the scheduler level).\n42\t- Integrate the scheduler plugin with the queueing layer's admission flow so quota and admission decisions remain at the queueing layer while gang semantics are enforced at scheduling time, for both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n43\t- Configure group sizing and timeout behavior so jobs that cannot be fully placed are released and requeued rather than holding partial allocations.\n44\t- Validate gang admission end-to-end for PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads at representative multi-node GPU sizes under queue contention, at the scale the native path was found insufficient.\n45\t- Rollback safety: the scheduler-plugin change is configuration-based and reversible so the platform scheduler can be restored to its default configuration.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- With the coscheduling plugin enabled, a multi-node PyTorchJob or RayJob is scheduled as a group: no partial GPU occupation is observed while waiting for remaining pods, verified at target scale under queue contention.\n50\t- Quota and admission decisions remain enforced by the queueing layer (per-project GPU quota still gates admission) with the plugin active.\n51\t- Jobs that cannot be fully placed within the configured group timeout are released and requeued without holding partial allocations.\n52\t- The scheduler configuration change is reversible: disabling the plugin restores default scheduling behavior without requiring code rollback.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-1 (P0): Multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing — primary coverage, via the scheduler-plugin path selected by the gang-admission investigation.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97427b6cdc973e21","agent_id":"a8f861f4d9cfa2f37","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"8a584e2b-bfbb-444b-b690-caff6c7664d0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:29:45.826Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8643790898e1c3cc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
