selected semantics).\n43\t- Apply preemption to PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads admitted through the queueing layer.\n44\t- Provide admin configuration for the preemption policy (priority rules, requeue behavior).\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- A higher-priority training workload preempts a lower-priority one according to the admin-defined policy, for both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n49\t- A preempted workload is fully evicted (no orphaned pods or leaked GPU allocations) and requeued, and is re-admitted when capacity/quota permits.\n50\t- Admins can define and change the preemption policy, and changes take effect on subsequent preemption decisions.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-4 (P1): Higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones according to an admin-defined policy — primary coverage, via the eviction-with-requeue semantics selected by the preemption investigation.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97427b6cdc973e21","agent_id":"a8f861f4d9cfa2f37","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"0cddbbc8-10a7-4eed-ac2f-5fca8ba6c2b7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:29:46.958Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5afee324ac0c1f7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
