{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b10af0f4f6918141","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: PyTorchJob checkpoint/restart support for graceful preemption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E008\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If full eviction with requeue is sufficient, PyTorchJob checkpoint/restart\n17\t    support for graceful preemption is not needed and this branch epic is dropped.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# PyTorchJob checkpoint/restart support for graceful preemption\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis branch epic delivers PyTorchJob checkpoint and restart-from-checkpoint support in the training operator, required by the checkpoint-aware graceful preemption path selected when the preemption-semantics investigation determines customers need graceful preemption. When a PyTorchJob is gracefully preempted, its state is checkpointed; when requeued and re-admitted, it resumes from that checkpoint. It builds against the graceful-preemption coordination provided by the queueing layer in this same outcome.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Support checkpoint initiation for PyTorchJob workloads on the graceful-preemption signal from the queueing layer: the job's training state is saved within the configured grace period.\n43\t- Support restart-from-checkpoint when a preempted PyTorchJob is re-admitted, resuming training from the last checkpoint rather than from scratch.\n44\t- Cover multi-node PyTorchJob topologies at representative GPU sizes.\n45\t- Define checkpoint storage/retention requirements for preempted jobs (where checkpoints live and how long they are kept for resume), consistent with the checkpoint-overhead benchmark from the preemption investigation.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A gracefully preempted PyTorchJob produces a usable checkpoint within the grace period, including multi-node topologies.\n50\t- A re-admitted PyTorchJob resumes training from its checkpoint (verified by resumed-step/loss continuity versus a from-scratch run), including multi-node topologies.\n51\t- Checkpoint storage and retention behave per the defined requirements (preempted jobs' checkpoints are available for resume and expire per retention policy).\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-4 (P1): Higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones according to an admin-defined policy — provides the PyTorchJob checkpoint/restart capability the checkpoint-aware preemption semantics depend on.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97427b6cdc973e21","agent_id":"a8f861f4d9cfa2f37","session_id":"f72e5a6b-50db-4e86-b979-c3cde993f59c","uuid":"4a9f9989-1bb8-4975-a103-4bb76436ca3f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:29:49.599Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b10af0f4f6918141","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
